When the robot leans forwards, this code prints the difference between 90° and the angle instead of the angle (at a 30° tilt it shows 60°). Which line is wrong?

```
1  float ax = axHam / 16384.0;
2  float az = azHam / 16384.0;
3  float aci = atan2(az, ax) * 57.2958;
4  float hiz = gyHam / 65.5;     // ±500 °/s aralığı
```

The bias measured at start-up is 1.8 °/s. While the robot is still, a raw gyHam = 262 is read (65.5 counts/(°/s)). What does this code print?

```
float sapma = 1.8;
int16_t gyHam = 262;
float hiz = gyHam / 65.5 - sapma;
Serial.println(hiz, 2);
```
